id: pm-gh1607
title: "GH-1607: Provide intent-specific recovery for unsupported block and unblock commands"
description: "**Version:** pm 2026.10.26.\n\n**Repro**\n```sh\npm block <id> --reason waiting\npm unblock <id> --note ready\n```\n**Observed:** both exit 2. `block` suggests `github blockers` and `list --status blocked` (read-only surfaces); `unblock` prints generic examples (`activity`, `aggregate`, `assurance`, …). Neither points at the supported local mutation.\n\n**Expected:** intent-specific recovery for these lifecycle verbs, e.g.\n```sh\npm update <id> --blocked-by <blocker> --blocked-reason \"waiting\"\npm update <id> --dep-remove <blocker> --unset blocked_by --unset blocked_reason --unblock-note \"ready\"\n```\nor first-class `block`/`unblock` aliases that map to those flags (never auto-executing a guessed mutation).\n\n**Why it matters for agents:** block/unblock are the verbs agents reach for during a work session; today the failed call is followed by a help search and another attempt (~600–750 bytes of unhelpful stderr each). Note that `--unblock-note` alone records a note but does not remove the blocker edge, which is easy to get wrong without a worked example.\n\n\nIntake boundary: this is a report against published 2026.10.26, not proof of a current-checkout defect. Reproduce in an external sandbox before implementation. Related completed work retains its shipped scope. Proposed examples or categories are not accepted contracts until validated.\n\nSource: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1607"
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[3]: agent-ux,github,sdk
created_at: "2026-10-26T19:02:14.338Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-27T03:35:44.271Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-26T23:58:46.714Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-26T23:58:46.714Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: "Derive examples from live update contracts and prove the suggested block and unblock workflows on isolated trackers.; Unblock recovery explains removal of the actual blocker relationship and stale blocker metadata; a note alone is not presented as unblocking.; Refusals preserve the usage exit code, leave data unchanged, identify the intended lifecycle surface, and retain extension-command and ambiguity behavior. Any new alias must have a declared SDK/CLI/MCP contract."
parent: pm-f05lsg
risk: low
confidence: medium
resolution: Expose SDK-owned lifecycle recovery templates and scoped inspection guidance for unsupported block and unblock verbs.
expected_result: Unsupported verbs refuse without mutation and explain declared update flags; the unblock template clears all blockers and stale reasons while preserving unrelated relationships.
actual_result: "Linked19-test cohort passes; real command templates remove both blocker edges while preserving the unrelated related edge, and refusals leave history unchanged. Hosted native Windows regression, complete exact coverage and every packed first-run check pass at58e8f1226. First-head static planner metadata failure is corrected locally; revised-head required checks and review remain pre-merge gates."
